<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

	<!--
		The six insect mamono xenotypes. Every one carries ProjectMamono_Mamono +
		PMM_Gene_Insect (chitin, feelers) and is inheritable, all-female and excluded
		from the factionless spawner (factionlessGenerationWeight 0 - they only enter
		the world in the two insector tribes). The bulk of each species' stats lives
		on its race def (Races_InsectMamono_BS.xml); the genes here add the MGE
		flavour on top. Gene defNames verified against Core/Biotech 1.6.

		Each xenotype also declares its race with Big & Small's XenotypeExtension
		(setRace). That is the only link between a species' genes and its race def,
		and it matters because the race def holds the real physiology: temperature
		range, body size, melee tools and race abilities such as the abaddon's
		egg-spew. Big & Small applies the field when a pawn is GENERATED; PMM core
		re-applies it when a woman is transformed into one of these xenotypes at
		runtime, so a corrupted woman becomes the species properly instead of
		wearing its genes on a baseliner body.

		forceRace is on for all six: without it, a mere gene request for a winged
		body (the flight genes carry one) can win the swap over the species race,
		and the pawn ends up as a plain winged human with no species at all.
	-->

	<!-- Devil Bug (megascarab): a dim, short-lived hive builder of the swarm -->
	<XenotypeDef>
		<defName>PMM_InsectDevilBug</defName>
		<label>devil bug</label>
		<description>A cockroach-like insect mamono of dark, damp places, and the lowest rung of the hive. She builds and mends the walls her sisters live in and hauls what they leave behind, and they treat her as little more than a household pest - which is exactly what she is. She does not mind the work, and she does not stop.</description>
		<descriptionShort>A cockroach-like drudge who raises and mends the hive's walls.</descriptionShort>
		<iconPath>UI/Icons/Xenotypes/PMM_DevilBug</iconPath>
		<inheritable>true</inheritable>
		<factionlessGenerationWeight>0</factionlessGenerationWeight>
		<genes>
			<li>ProjectMamono_Mamono</li>
			<li>PMM_Gene_Insect</li>
			<!-- The other castes carry this in their insect package: antennae that
			     actually render. Vanilla-side it is a plain cosmetic GeneDef
			     (`GeneDefs_Cosmetic.xml`: label "insect antennae", `randomChosen`,
			     1 complexity, no stat effect, not a geneline pick), so it leaves the
			     3/3 balance below alone. Her own insect gene only *describes* feelers. -->
			<li>VRE_InsectAntennae</li>
			<!-- The user's package of 2026-09-27, replacing her launch set. Three
			     evolutions (hive glands, swarm synapse, infrared sensors) and three
			     degrades (low grey matter, rapid life cycle, microsized) - three and
			     three, the balance VRE's own picker demands (VRE_NeedEqualAmount).
			     Hive glands is what lets a mamono raise VFEI2 hives at all (HANDOFF
			     §7.1), and that is the point of her now: the swarm's builder. Swarm
			     synapse, infrared sensors and microsized are pherocore-locked, so
			     recruiting her is what unlocks them for the player (§5.3 rule 4).
			     Her prices are a drone's head and a drone's life: low grey matter
			     leaves her dim, rapid life cycle short-lived, and microsized takes a
			     flat 0.45 off her body size. -->
			<li>VRE_Hiveglands</li>
			<li>VRE_SwarmSynapse</li>
			<li>VRE_InfraredSensors</li>
			<li>VRE_LowGreyMatter</li>
			<li>VRE_RapidLifeCycle</li>
			<li>VRE_Microsized</li>
			<!-- Vanilla aptitudes in the user's words: "good construction" is
			     AptitudeStrong_Construction, "awful intellect" is
			     AptitudeTerrible_Intellectual and "poor social" is AptitudePoor_Social.
			     Vanilla builds these from templates (AptitudeStrong, AptitudeTerrible
			     and AptitudePoor in Data/Biotech/Defs/GeneDefs/GeneTemplateDefs.xml),
			     so no such def exists in any file - the game makes one per skill at
			     load. The labels are vanilla's own: "good", "awful", "poor". -->
			<li>AptitudeStrong_Construction</li>
			<li>AptitudeTerrible_Intellectual</li>
			<li>AptitudePoor_Social</li>
			<!-- A drone of the swarm does not breed (user ruling 2026-09-27): vanilla's
			     `Sterile` (Fertility x0, `sterilize`, 1 metabolism, plain GeneDef), the
			     same gene the queen carries. It is not a geneline pick, so the 3/3
			     balance above is untouched, and it is the whole lock - no race stat and
			     no hediff. What makes it bite lives in the core mod, not here:
			     `MamonoFertilityPatch.DeliberatelySterile` stands aside for a pawn whose
			     barrenness is deliberate, so the vanilla gene is enough. The swarm grows
			     by the queen's egg sac, not by her drones. -->
			<li>Sterile</li>
		</genes>
		<modExtensions>
			<li Class="BigAndSmall.XenotypeExtension">
				<setRace>PMM_Race_DevilBug</setRace>
				<forceRace>true</forceRace>
			</li>
			<li Class="PMM_Insects.InsectSkinColours">
				<colours>
					<li>PMM_Skin_DevilBugCharred</li>
					<li>PMM_Skin_DevilBugWalnut</li>
					<li>PMM_Skin_DevilBugHazel</li>
				</colours>
			</li>
		</modExtensions>
	</XenotypeDef>

	<!-- Giant Ant (spelopede): diligent worker, digging claws, great strength -->
	<XenotypeDef>
		<defName>PMM_InsectGiantAnt</defName>
		<label>giant ant</label>
		<description>A worker caste mamono of the deep nests. Honest and diligent, she digs through solid rock and carries loads larger than herself without complaint - though the pheromones in her sweat grow heavier the harder she works.</description>
		<descriptionShort>A diligent, strong insect mamono born to dig and haul.</descriptionShort>
		<iconPath>UI/Icons/Xenotypes/PMM_GiantAnt</iconPath>
		<inheritable>true</inheritable>
		<factionlessGenerationWeight>0</factionlessGenerationWeight>
		<genes>
			<li>ProjectMamono_Mamono</li>
			<li>PMM_Gene_Insect</li>
			<!-- Antennae: the same cosmetic gene the other castes carry. -->
			<li>VRE_InsectAntennae</li>
			<!-- The user's package of 2026-09-27, replacing her launch set. Three
			     evolutions (her digging horn, swarm synapse, robust midgut) and three
			     degrades (low grey matter, rapid life cycle, microsized) - three and
			     three, the balance VRE's picker demands (VRE_NeedEqualAmount). Swarm
			     synapse and microsized are pherocore-locked, so recruiting her unlocks
			     two of VFEI2's boss rewards (§5.3 rule 4). Hive glands left her with
			     this package: §5.3 now names the greenworm, the ant arachne and the
			     devil bug as the castes that raise hives. -->
			<li>VRE_SpelopedeHorn</li>
			<li>VRE_SwarmSynapse</li>
			<li>VRE_RobustMidgut</li>
			<li>VRE_LowGreyMatter</li>
			<li>VRE_RapidLifeCycle</li>
			<li>VRE_Microsized</li>
			<!-- Vanilla genes in the user's words: "good mining" is
			     AptitudeStrong_Mining, "awful intellect" AptitudeTerrible_Intellectual,
			     "poor social" AptitudePoor_Social, "low sleep" vanilla's own LowSleep
			     (RestFallRateFactor 0.4), and "sterile" vanilla's Sterile - the same
			     barren lock the queen and the devil bug carry, which works because
			     core's MomoFertilityPatch stands aside for a deliberate sterility. She
			     is the tribe's strong, tireless digger: dumb as a rock, and unable to
			     bear young of her own. -->
			<li>AptitudeStrong_Mining</li>
			<li>AptitudeTerrible_Intellectual</li>
			<li>AptitudePoor_Social</li>
			<li>LowSleep</li>
			<li>Sterile</li>
		</genes>
		<modExtensions>
			<li Class="BigAndSmall.XenotypeExtension">
				<setRace>PMM_Race_GiantAnt</setRace>
				<forceRace>true</forceRace>
			</li>
			<li Class="PMM_Insects.InsectSkinColours">
				<colours>
					<li>PMM_Skin_AntIndigo</li>
					<li>PMM_Skin_AntSlate</li>
					<li>PMM_Skin_AntSky</li>
				</colours>
			</li>
		</modExtensions>
	</XenotypeDef>

	<!-- Soldier Beetle (megaspider): heavy armour, ripper blades, hidden wings -->
	<XenotypeDef>
		<defName>PMM_InsectSoldierBeetle</defName>
		<label>soldier beetle</label>
		<description>Heavy cavalry from birth. Her exoskeleton turns aside swords and arrows, her claws are ripper-blades, and hidden beneath the carapace on her back are wings for short bursts of flight. Calm, obedient and nearly expressionless - until she chooses a man to escort.</description>
		<descriptionShort>An armoured, obedient insect mamono with ripper claws and hidden wings.</descriptionShort>
		<iconPath>UI/Icons/Xenotypes/PMM_SoldierBeetle</iconPath>
		<inheritable>true</inheritable>
		<factionlessGenerationWeight>0</factionlessGenerationWeight>
		<genes>
			<li>ProjectMamono_Mamono</li>
			<li>PMM_Gene_Insect</li>
			<li>Robust</li>
			<li>PMM_Gene_FlightWeak</li>
			<!-- Large frame (core): the heavy cavalry frame that carries more. She
			     is a weak flyer, not a strong one, so the two genes do not clash. -->
			<li>PMM_Gene_LargeFrame</li>
			<li>MeleeDamage_Strong</li>
			<!-- VRE Insector (HANDOFF §5.3): HardenedChitin turns aside a quarter of
			     all incoming damage and CuticleShell shrugs off common disease. That
			     much body costs her: InefficientMidgut means she must eat far more,
			     and Stenothermic means she only thrives in her own climate. Two and
			     two. -->
			<li>VRE_HardenedChitin</li>
			<li>VRE_CuticleShell</li>
			<li>VRE_InefficientMidgut</li>
			<li>VRE_Stenothermic</li>
			<li>VRE_InsectJellyDependency</li>
		</genes>
		<modExtensions>
			<li Class="BigAndSmall.XenotypeExtension">
				<setRace>PMM_Race_SoldierBeetle</setRace>
				<forceRace>true</forceRace>
			</li>
			<li Class="PMM_Insects.InsectSkinColours">
				<colours>
					<li>PMM_Skin_BeetleDark</li>
					<li>PMM_Skin_BeetleTaupe</li>
					<li>PMM_Skin_BeetleSoot</li>
				</colours>
			</li>
		</modExtensions>
	</XenotypeDef>

	<!-- Greenworm (larva): soft, gentle, slow, acid secretion -->
	<XenotypeDef>
		<defName>PMM_InsectGreenworm</defName>
		<label>greenworm</label>
		<description>A soft-bodied, gentle mamono who loves nothing more than eating. Her antennae secrete a strange-smelling substance that saps the strength of anything that threatens her - and she spits the same sludge in fright.</description>
		<descriptionShort>A soft, gentle insect mamono who spits acidic sludge.</descriptionShort>
		<iconPath>UI/Icons/Xenotypes/PMM_Greenworm</iconPath>
		<inheritable>true</inheritable>
		<factionlessGenerationWeight>0</factionlessGenerationWeight>
		<genes>
			<li>ProjectMamono_Mamono</li>
			<li>PMM_Gene_Insect</li>
			<!-- The user's package of 2026-09-27, replacing her launch set. Every gene
			     here is a degrade and none is an evolution: the hand-kept
			     evolution/degrade balance the geneline UI asks for is deliberately
			     broken, because she is the swarm's most useless caste. Porous skin,
			     weakened chitin and immunodeficiency make her a soft bag of flesh that
			     catches everything; passive means she will not fight at all (the
			     user's "docile"); microsized shrinks her; an inefficient midgut always
			     wants more; low grey matter is the head she has. Passive and
			     microsized are pherocore-locked, so recruiting her unlocks two of
			     VFEI2's boss rewards (§5.3 rule 4). The jelly gene is a reversal: she
			     used to be the one caste exempt from it as brood. -->
			<li>VRE_Immunodeficiency</li>
			<li>VRE_PorousSkin</li>
			<li>VRE_WeakenedChitin</li>
			<li>VRE_PassiveInsect</li>
			<li>VRE_Microsized</li>
			<li>VRE_InefficientMidgut</li>
			<li>VRE_LowGreyMatter</li>
			<li>VRE_InsectAntennae</li>
			<li>VRE_InsectJellyDependency</li>
			<!-- Vanilla genes: "low intellect" is AptitudeTerrible_Intellectual, and
			     "sterile" is vanilla's Sterile - the same lock the queen, the devil
			     bug and the giant ant carry. -->
			<li>AptitudeTerrible_Intellectual</li>
			<li>Sterile</li>
		</genes>
		<modExtensions>
			<li Class="BigAndSmall.XenotypeExtension">
				<setRace>PMM_Race_Greenworm</setRace>
				<forceRace>true</forceRace>
			</li>
			<li Class="PMM_Insects.InsectSkinColours">
				<colours>
					<li>PMM_Skin_WormPale</li>
					<li>PMM_Skin_WormLeaf</li>
					<li>PMM_Skin_WormDeep</li>
				</colours>
			</li>
		</modExtensions>
	</XenotypeDef>

	<!-- Vamp Mosquito (locust): thin buzzing wings and weak flight (no
	     caravan speed, no passenger), venomous bite, blood-drinking -->
	<XenotypeDef>
		<defName>PMM_InsectVampMosquito</defName>
		<label>vamp mosquito</label>
		<description>The vampire of the insect world. Cunning and mean, she stalks her prey on buzzing wings and strikes when their guard drops. Her bite carries a venom that makes the wound hot and throbbing - and only her touch soothes it. She drinks blood most greedily in her lover's arms.</description>
		<descriptionShort>A winged, blood-drinking insect mamono with a venomous bite.</descriptionShort>
		<iconPath>UI/Icons/Xenotypes/PMM_VampMosquito</iconPath>
		<inheritable>true</inheritable>
		<factionlessGenerationWeight>0</factionlessGenerationWeight>
		<genes>
			<li>ProjectMamono_Mamono</li>
			<li>PMM_Gene_Insect</li>
			<li>PMM_Gene_FlightWeak</li>
			<!-- Rebuilt on the user's list, 2026-09-27; the old set is scrapped. "Generic insect
			     package" is three things here: the pheromones are PMM_Gene_Insect's job (our
			     InsectPheromones.cs copies VRE's two patches and keys them to our gene), so VRE's
			     bare VRE_InsectPheromones flag is deliberately NOT listed - one flag per feature,
			     as with the beelzebub - and the other two are the antennae and the jelly
			     dependency below. -->
			<li>VRE_InfraredSensors</li>
			<li>VRE_HighGreyMatter</li>
			<li>VRE_Microsized</li>
			<li>VRE_WeakenedChitin</li>
			<li>VRE_InsectAntennae</li>
			<li>VRE_InsectJellyDependency</li>
			<!-- The blood trio, and none of it is VRE: all three are vanilla Biotech genes off
			     the sanguophage. Hemogenic is the hemogen bar itself (2 hemogen a day lost to
			     biological entropy); Bloodfeeder is the Bloodfeed ability and names Hemogenic as
			     its prerequisite, which is why the two travel together; Coagulate is the
			     wound-tending ability - her hands close a wound, which is the "only her touch
			     soothes it" half of her lore. Note what is NOT here: vanilla's HemogenDrain, the
			     need that makes an empty bar dangerous. As listed she can drink blood and never
			     must, so add HemogenDrain if she should be driven to it. -->
			<li>Hemogenic</li>
			<li>Bloodfeeder</li>
			<li>Coagulate</li>
			<!-- Blood rush (user, 2026-09-27). Core's own gene, and it fits her better
			     than anyone: it needs Hemogenic, which she carries, and while her
			     hemogen sits at 75% or more she is 15% faster on her feet and 15%
			     faster between melee attacks. The cost is a flat 2 hemogen a day on
			     top of Hemogenic's own 2, so her bar burns at 4 a day and she feeds
			     twice as often. It is a core gene, not a VRE geneline one, so it does
			     not touch her evolution/mutation count. -->
			<li>PMM_Gene_BloodRush</li>
			<!-- Scrapped with the old set: VRE_AcidBlood (toxic gas when she is cut),
			     VRE_AntimicrobialPeptides (self-mending) and vanilla Beauty_Beautiful. -->
		</genes>
		<modExtensions>
			<li Class="BigAndSmall.XenotypeExtension">
				<setRace>PMM_Race_VampMosquito</setRace>
				<forceRace>true</forceRace>
			</li>
			<li Class="PMM_Insects.InsectSkinColours">
				<colours>
					<li>PMM_Skin_MosquitoCharcoal</li>
					<li>PMM_Skin_MosquitoPale</li>
					<li>PMM_Skin_MosquitoAsh</li>
				</colours>
			</li>
		</modExtensions>
	</XenotypeDef>

	<!-- Abaddon (hive queen): the devouring queen, never sleeps, egg-spew -->
	<XenotypeDef>
		<defName>PMM_InsectAbaddon</defName>
		<label>abaddon</label>
		<description>Daughter of the bug mamono lord who nearly devoured the world in antiquity. Quiet and spacey rather than ferocious, but her appetite - and her fertility - are without limit. Her pheromones command the swarm, her wingbeats shake the heavens, and once she devotes herself to a man it is for life.</description>
		<descriptionShort>A sleepless queen mamono of limitless appetite and fertility.</descriptionShort>
		<iconPath>UI/Icons/Xenotypes/PMM_Abaddon</iconPath>
		<inheritable>true</inheritable>
		<factionlessGenerationWeight>0</factionlessGenerationWeight>
		<genes>
			<li>ProjectMamono_Mamono</li>
			<li>PMM_Gene_Insect</li>
			<li>PMM_Gene_Flight</li>
			<li>AptitudeStrong_Intellectual</li>
			<!-- The royal package, reworked to the user's list of 2026-09-26, then two more
			     passes the same day. The gifts: swarm synapse (the hive mind), slowed life
			     cycle (she never ages), vocal glands (a human voice, and a song most people
			     call beautiful), robust midgut (raw food feeds her properly and never
			     sickens her) and her sheer size. The costs: colossal hunger, dormancy,
			     hard-locked joints and a body that sleeps through the cold.

			     Four evolutions against four mutations, the 4/4 §5.3 asks for, held across
			     every pass by swapping like for like: the inefficient midgut out for the
			     stiff joints (she pays for her size with a slow walk, not a bottomless
			     stomach), then parthenogenesis out for the robust midgut. She conceives no
			     children at all now - the vanilla `Sterile` gene below sees to that - so her
			     egg sac is the only way to more abaddons (§5.11). Sterile is a plain vanilla
			     GeneDef, not one of VRE's pools, so it costs the 4/4 nothing: it pays 1
			     metabolism instead, and it takes the `Fertility` tag back that
			     parthenogenesis gave up. What makes it bite is the core mod's
			     `MamonoFertilityPatch.DeliberatelySterile`, not anything in this mod.

			     Gone from her old package along the way: the spawning sack, protein
			     denaturation (sunlight burned her) and the two genes swapped above. She
			     keeps to the dark because she wants to now, not because the sun forbids it. -->
			<li>VRE_SwarmSynapse</li>
			<li>VRE_RobustMidgut</li>
			<li>VRE_SlowedLifeCycle</li>
			<li>VRE_VocalGlands</li>
			<li>VRE_Colossal</li>
			<li>VRE_Dormant</li>
			<li>VRE_HardLockedJoints</li>
			<li>VRE_HypothermicHibernation</li>
			<li>VRE_InsectJellyDependency</li>
			<!-- No natural children, ever: vanilla's `Sterile` (Fertility x0, `sterilize`,
			     1 metabolism). It holds the shared `Fertility` exclusion tag, it explains itself
			     in her gene list, and it is the whole lock - no race stat, no hediff, no extra
			     gene. What makes it bite lives in the core mod, not here: the Mamono fertility
			     protection used to hold every mamono at 100% whatever her genes said, and
			     `MamonoFertilityPatch.DeliberatelySterile` now stands aside for a pawn whose
			     barrenness is deliberate - a gene with `sterilize`, or a hediff that prevents
			     pregnancy. Vanilla's own words for the gene - "Carriers of this gene cannot
			     reproduce by natural means" - are true of her. -->
			<li>Sterile</li>
			<!-- Body, head and antennae: the same two genes her soldier daughters carry,
			     and they do not collide with her body colour (body/fur tags against the
			     colour's vanilla SkinColorOverride - see the folk's note). -->
			<li>VRE_InsectSkin</li>
			<li>VRE_InsectAntennae</li>
			<!-- Her abdomen. The real spawning sack is out on a tag, as it always was: the
			     shared `Fertility` tag it fights over is held by `Sterile` now instead of by
			     parthenogenesis. VRE ships the look alone as VRE_SpawningSack_Cosmetic: same
			     attachment node, same texture, same skin-colour tint, and no stat work at
			     all. Its one exclusion tag is `Tail`, so it would clash with a tail gene -
			     and she has none. Pure looks: the sacks say what she is without doing
			     anything. -->
			<li>VRE_SpawningSack_Cosmetic</li>
		</genes>
		<modExtensions>
			<li Class="BigAndSmall.XenotypeExtension">
				<setRace>PMM_Race_Abaddon</setRace>
				<forceRace>true</forceRace>
			</li>
			<li Class="PMM_Insects.InsectSkinColours">
				<colours>
					<li>PMM_Skin_AbaddonMauve</li>
					<li>PMM_Skin_AbaddonDove</li>
					<li>PMM_Skin_AbaddonSoot</li>
				</colours>
			</li>
		</modExtensions>
	</XenotypeDef>

	<!-- Abaddon Folk (soldier bugs): the swarm's infantry, and the seventh species
	     here. No spawn source: no pawn group and no faction roster names her, so read
	     the header on PMM_Race_AbaddonFolk in Defs/ThingDefs/Races_InsectMamono_BS.xml
	     before giving her one. Her pawn kind
	     (Defs/PawnKindDefs/PawnKinds_AbaddonFolk.xml) exists so she can be spawned by
	     name - dev mode and the like - rather than only converted out of someone else.
	     Both ways give the body: core's XenotypeRacePatch applies the race a xenotype
	     declares whenever a living pawn is given one, which is what used to be missing
	     when this species was tested through dev "apply xenotype".

	     Her gene list is the user's list of 2026-09-25. Two notes on where it
	     differs from a literal reading of it:

	     * "Insect pheromones" is covered by PMM_Gene_Insect, which carries the
	       behaviour itself (Source/Insects/InsectPheromones.cs), so VRE's
	       VRE_InsectPheromones is deliberately absent - it is a bare flag whose two
	       Harmony patches are the ones we copied. Listing it would add a second
	       copy of one thing and read as live support for a feature nobody owns.
	     * "Insect skin" is VRE's VRE_InsectSkin, the user's call, taken knowing it
	       overrides the skin with VRE's insect body and forces one of VRE's
	       four insect head shapes. It does not cost her the body colour: its fur is
	       drawn with the pawn's skin colour (`useSkinColorForFur` in its
	       VEF.Genes.GeneExtension), so her shell still takes the colour she rolled.

	     Balance follows VRE's own geneline rule, two evolutions against two
	     degrades: swarm synapse and hardened chitin against microsized and
	     inefficient midgut. The jelly dependency and the cosmetic antennae sit
	     outside that count. -->
	<XenotypeDef>
		<defName>PMM_InsectAbaddonFolk</defName>
		<label>abaddon folk</label>
		<description>One of the countless soldier bugs of an abaddon's swarm. Petite where her queen is vast, she is built for the swarm rather than for herself: she reads the swarm's orders in the pheromones in the air, shares her sisters' endless hunger for jelly, and once she has a man for her own she tends him as calmly and as constantly as she tends her post.</description>
		<descriptionShort>A petite soldier bug of the abaddon swarm, who lives by pheromones.</descriptionShort>
		<!-- Placeholder: the queen's crest, until she has art of her own. It is the
		     same family, and a missing path would only log a texture error. -->
		<iconPath>UI/Icons/Xenotypes/PMM_Abaddon</iconPath>
		<inheritable>true</inheritable>
		<factionlessGenerationWeight>0</factionlessGenerationWeight>
		<genes>
			<li>ProjectMamono_Mamono</li>
			<!-- The mod's own insect gene: chitin skin and base tone, feelers, full
			     toxin immunity, insect flesh as her own kind's meat, and the pheromones
			     that keep wild insectoids off her. -->
			<li>PMM_Gene_Insect</li>
			<!-- Two evolutions and two degrades, the geneline balance VRE's own
			     picker demands. SwarmSynapse is the linked hive mind; HardenedChitin
			     turns a quarter of every hit; Microsized makes her the smallest thing
			     in the swarm; InefficientMidgut is the appetite that pays for the
			     other three. -->
			<li>VRE_SwarmSynapse</li>
			<li>VRE_HardenedChitin</li>
			<li>VRE_Microsized</li>
			<li>VRE_InefficientMidgut</li>
			<!-- Jelly on the fighting castes only. She is one of them. -->
			<li>VRE_InsectJellyDependency</li>
			<!-- Body, head and antennae. Two gene groups, and they do not collide:
			     VRE_InsectSkin's exclusion tags are body and fur tags, while the chitin
			     tone she rolls (the roll lives on PMM_Gene_Insect - see
			     Source/Insects/InsectChitin.cs) carries vanilla's SkinColorOverride
			     tag, so neither group touches the other. The antennae gene is
			     randomChosen too, but nothing else here shares its Antenna tags, so it
			     simply stays. -->
			<li>VRE_InsectSkin</li>
			<li>VRE_InsectAntennae</li>
			<!-- Weak flight, the same gene the soldier beetle and the vamp mosquito
			     carry: she flies in short bursts, so she is no caravan mount and carries
			     no passenger. -->
			<li>PMM_Gene_FlightWeak</li>
			<!-- Poor at talking - she answers to the swarm, not to people. An aptitude
			     changes how fast she learns to deal with others, not how good she is at
			     it today. -->
			<li>AptitudePoor_Social</li>
			<!-- Great at fighting, by contrast: +8 melee aptitude and a passion level,
			     so a soldier bug is born knowing her trade (user, 2026-09-25). Both
			     aptitudes sit outside the evolution/degrade count. -->
			<li>AptitudeRemarkable_Melee</li>

		</genes>
		<modExtensions>
			<li Class="BigAndSmall.XenotypeExtension">
				<setRace>PMM_Race_AbaddonFolk</setRace>
				<forceRace>true</forceRace>
			</li>
			<li Class="PMM_Insects.InsectSkinColours">
				<colours>
					<li>PMM_Skin_AbaddonFolkRose</li>
					<li>PMM_Skin_AbaddonFolkPlum</li>
					<li>PMM_Skin_AbaddonFolkHeather</li>
				</colours>
			</li>
		</modExtensions>
	</XenotypeDef>

	<!-- ===================== Arachne (2026-09-26) ===================== -->
	<!-- Species identity through aptitudes and VRE's insect kit, with B&S's spider body
	     forced at generation through XenotypeExtension/setRace - the same route the folk
	     xenotype above uses, so a generated pawn and dev "apply xenotype" both end up with
	     eight legs (core's XenotypeRacePatch covers the dev path).

	     Deliberately NOT on her: VRE_InsectSkin and VRE_InsectAntennae, which the swarm's
	     other species wear. Her upper body is the spider's own art
	     (BS_SpooderGraphicSetUpper), and an insect fur body or insect head would fight it.
	     She stays an insect mamono through PMM_Gene_Insect - insect flesh, feelers, toxin
	     immunity, the shared skin base - and the chitin colour it rolls for her.

	     Look variant: settled 2026-09-26. B&S ships no Synthread and no Devilstrand body gene -
	     those two names appear only in its own gene-page settings and have no def behind them in
	     this install (the user checked in game) - and the stock spider body renders clean, so
	     there is no variant to add and none to fake.

	     Tribe-only: factionlessGenerationWeight 0, so she never turns up in a random pawn
	     or a factionless event. Her spawn table entry and the line that lets an abaddon lay
	     her come next; until then she is reachable in dev mode. -->
	<XenotypeDef>
		<defName>PMM_InsectArachne</defName>
		<label>arachne</label>
		<description>A weaver of the deep dark, patient and cruel, with eight legs and a silk sac.</description>
		<inheritable>true</inheritable>
		<factionlessGenerationWeight>0</factionlessGenerationWeight>
		<genes>
			<li>ProjectMamono_Mamono</li>
			<li>PMM_Gene_Insect</li>
			<!-- A big spider is a caravan animal (user's call 2026-09-26): core's large frame,
			     the same gene the soldier beetle carries. 20% for any caravan she joins, and
			     caravans count her as a riding animal. It changes no size stat, so her race's
			     1.3 pair is untouched, and its PMM_CaravanCarrier tag costs nothing here
			     because she carries no flight gene. -->
			<li>PMM_Gene_LargeFrame</li>
			<!-- The mind and the hands of a weaver: good, not great - user vocabulary
			     2026-09-26, "good" is AptitudeStrong and "great" is AptitudeRemarkable. -->
			<li>VRE_HighGreyMatter</li>
			<li>AptitudeStrong_Intellectual</li>
			<li>AptitudeStrong_Crafting</li>
			<li>AptitudePoor_Animals</li>
			<li>AptitudePoor_Plants</li>
			<!-- The voice, and the moods that come with it. -->
			<li>VRE_VocalGlands</li>
			<li>VRE_InsectVolatile</li>
			<!-- A creature of the dark: sunlight burns her, and the hive's jelly feeds her. -->
			<li>VRE_ProteinDenaturation</li>
			<li>VRE_InsectJellyDependency</li>
		</genes>
		<modExtensions>
			<li Class="BigAndSmall.XenotypeExtension">
				<setRace>PMM_Race_Arachne</setRace>
				<forceRace>true</forceRace>
			</li>
			<li Class="PMM_Insects.InsectSkinColours">
				<colours>
					<li>PMM_Skin_ArachneLavender</li>
					<li>PMM_Skin_ArachneSlate</li>
					<li>PMM_Skin_ArachneDeep</li>
				</colours>
			</li>
		</modExtensions>
	</XenotypeDef>

	<!-- The fly (2026-09-27). The user's gene list, in their order, with the defName each one
	     actually is in this load order: "sensitive brain" is VRE's sensitive brain goop, "fast
	     movement" is vanilla's MoveSpeed_VeryQuick, "enhanced psychic sensitivity" is vanilla's
	     PsychicAbility_Enhanced. Weak flight was asked for afterwards and comes from the core
	     mod, the same gene the soldier beetle and the vamp mosquito carry. Tribe-only like every
	     mamono here: factionlessGenerationWeight 0, and her spawn-table entries are in
	     Factions_InsectorTribes.xml, hostile tribe only. -->
	<XenotypeDef>
		<defName>PMM_InsectBeelzebub</defName>
		<label>beelzebub</label>
		<description>A lord of gluttony among the swarm's flies: tiny, quick, magically potent and always hungry.</description>
		<inheritable>true</inheritable>
		<factionlessGenerationWeight>0</factionlessGenerationWeight>
		<genes>
			<li>ProjectMamono_Mamono</li>
			<li>PMM_Gene_Insect</li>
			<!-- The eight the user asked for. -->
			<li>VRE_SensitiveBrainGoop</li>
			<li>VRE_RobustMidgut</li>
			<li>VRE_WeakenedChitin</li>
			<li>VRE_Microsized</li>
			<li>VRE_InsectJellyDependency</li>
			<li>VRE_InsectAntennae</li>
			<li>MoveSpeed_VeryQuick</li>
			<li>PsychicAbility_Enhanced</li>
			<!-- Weak flight (user, 2026-09-27). The core mod's own gene for thin wings: it lifts
			     only her, so she leaps a short way and carries nobody. This is the exact gene on
			     the soldier beetle and the vamp mosquito, wings and ability both. It also swaps
			     in the winged body and puts our small wings on her. -->
			<li>PMM_Gene_FlightWeak</li>
		</genes>
		<modExtensions>
			<li Class="BigAndSmall.XenotypeExtension">
				<setRace>PMM_Race_Beelzebub</setRace>
				<forceRace>true</forceRace>
			</li>
			<li Class="PMM_Insects.InsectSkinColours">
				<colours>
					<li>PMM_Skin_BeelzebubDark</li>
					<li>PMM_Skin_BeelzebubSlate</li>
					<li>PMM_Skin_BeelzebubPale</li>
				</colours>
			</li>
		</modExtensions>
	</XenotypeDef>

	<!-- The assassin of the desert (2026-09-27). Another arachne-family caste, built from the
	     user's gene list in their order. Three of the six are VRE's, read as VRE ships them:
	     "infrared sensors" is VRE_InfraredSensors, "charger claws" VRE_ChargerClaws (the charge
	     attack, not a stat), "compound eyes" the real VRE_CompoundEyes and not its cosmetic twin.
	     Two names needed settling. "hyperthermic slowdown" was read as VRE's cold gene, and the
	     user then asked for VRE_HypothermicHibernation in place of VRE_HypothermicSlowdown
	     (2026-09-27): she does not slow down in the cold, she goes under until it passes - no
	     frostbite, but nothing at all until she warms. "volatile" is VRE_InsectVolatile, the same
	     gene the arachne carries.

	     The swap also settles the count: hibernation is a mutation where slowdown was an
	     evolution, so she sits at three evolutions and three mutations - the same even split the
	     soldier beetle and the beelzebub keep at two and two, reached here by the user's choice
	     of gene rather than by trimming.

	     "Good melee" is AptitudeStrong_Melee - user vocabulary, "good" is Strong and "great" is
	     Remarkable. Vanilla builds these from the AptitudeStrong template, so there is no
	     AptitudeStrong_Melee def to find in the files; the game makes one per skill at load. -->
	<XenotypeDef>
		<defName>PMM_InsectGirtablilu</defName>
		<label>girtablilu</label>
		<description>An assassin of the desert: scorpion-shelled, pincer-handed and always ready to charge, with a sting's worth of venom in her claws.</description>
		<inheritable>true</inheritable>
		<factionlessGenerationWeight>0</factionlessGenerationWeight>
		<genes>
			<li>ProjectMamono_Mamono</li>
			<li>PMM_Gene_Insect</li>
			<!-- The six the user asked for. -->
			<li>VRE_InfraredSensors</li>
			<li>VRE_ChargerClaws</li>
			<li>VRE_CompoundEyes</li>
			<li>VRE_EcdysoneOverdrive</li>
			<li>VRE_InsectVolatile</li>
			<li>VRE_HypothermicHibernation</li>
			<!-- Good melee (user vocabulary): +4 aptitude, which is learning speed and starting
			     skill, not damage. Her damage is the pincers and the charge. -->
			<li>AptitudeStrong_Melee</li>
			<!-- Venom. This is core's own gene, the one the reptiles' basilisk carries -
			     ProjectMamono_MamonoVenom, with ProjectMamono_VenomBuildup's tingling-to-pinned
			     stages behind it. VenomDamagePatch watches for this gene on the attacker, so
			     every melee hit she lands injects it; she needs no stinger for that. -->
			<li>ProjectMamono_MamonoVenom</li>
		</genes>
		<modExtensions>
			<li Class="BigAndSmall.XenotypeExtension">
				<setRace>PMM_Race_Girtablilu</setRace>
				<forceRace>true</forceRace>
			</li>
			<li Class="PMM_Insects.InsectSkinColours">
				<colours>
					<li>PMM_Skin_GirtabliluTan</li>
					<li>PMM_Skin_GirtabliluSand</li>
					<li>PMM_Skin_GirtabliluRust</li>
				</colours>
			</li>
		</modExtensions>
	</XenotypeDef>

	<!-- The ant mimic (2026-09-27). An arachne the size of a worker, built from the
	     user's gene list in their order: vocal glands, hive glands, high grey
	     matter, microsized, dormant, rapid life cycle, insect antennae, good
	     construction.

	     "Good construction" is AptitudeStrong_Construction - user vocabulary, "good"
	     is Strong and "great" is Remarkable - and like the melee aptitude it is a
	     TEMPLATE gene: vanilla builds one per skill at load, so there is no def to
	     find in the files.

	     VRE_Hiveglands is the one that matters most for her: it is what lets a
	     momono build VFEI2's hive walls and jelly farms, and it carries +50%
	     construction speed on its own. She is the caste that builds the nest.

	     Dormant and rapid life cycle do not fight: rapid life cycle's exclusion tag
	     is InsectorLifespan (against SlowedLifeCycle), and dormant's is
	     InsectorAggression. Checked 2026-09-27.

	     No jelly dependency and no protein denaturation, the two genes her sister
	     has and she does not: the user's list is the list (2026-09-27). She lives
	     underground like an ant, so a sunlight penalty would have suited her - one
	     line if it should be added. -->
	<XenotypeDef>
		<defName>PMM_InsectAntArachne</defName>
		<label>ant arachne</label>
		<description>A small arachne disguised as a giant ant, living in the ants' own nest. Her hands are made for building, and the silk she spins is the same silk her bigger sister sells.</description>
		<inheritable>true</inheritable>
		<factionlessGenerationWeight>0</factionlessGenerationWeight>
		<genes>
			<li>ProjectMamono_Mamono</li>
			<li>PMM_Gene_Insect</li>
			<!-- The eight the user asked for. -->
			<li>VRE_VocalGlands</li>
			<li>VRE_Hiveglands</li>
			<li>VRE_HighGreyMatter</li>
			<li>VRE_Microsized</li>
			<li>VRE_Dormant</li>
			<li>VRE_RapidLifeCycle</li>
			<li>VRE_InsectAntennae</li>
			<li>AptitudeStrong_Construction</li>
		</genes>
		<modExtensions>
			<li Class="BigAndSmall.XenotypeExtension">
				<setRace>PMM_Race_AntArachne</setRace>
				<forceRace>true</forceRace>
			</li>
			<li Class="PMM_Insects.InsectSkinColours">
				<colours>
					<li>PMM_Skin_ArachneLavender</li>
					<li>PMM_Skin_ArachneSlate</li>
					<li>PMM_Skin_ArachneDeep</li>
				</colours>
			</li>
		</modExtensions>
	</XenotypeDef>

	<!-- Honey Bee (built 2026-09-27): the hive's farmer, and the one caste with honey -->
	<XenotypeDef>
		<defName>PMM_InsectHoneyBee</defName>
		<label>honey bee</label>
		<description>A honey bee mamono, round and soft and never still. She keeps the hive's crops and its beasts, humming to herself the whole time, and her body slowly fills with honey as she works. She is happiest doing exactly that, and there is little behind her eyes but the next row and the next animal.</description>
		<descriptionShort>A cheerful, tireless farmer whose body fills with honey.</descriptionShort>
		<iconPath>UI/Icons/Xenotypes/PMM_HoneyBee</iconPath>
		<inheritable>true</inheritable>
		<factionlessGenerationWeight>0</factionlessGenerationWeight>
		<genes>
			<li>ProjectMamono_Mamono</li>
			<li>PMM_Gene_Insect</li>
			<!-- Antennae: the same cosmetic gene the other castes carry. -->
			<li>VRE_InsectAntennae</li>
			<!-- Weak flight (core), in the user's list: she has wings and cannot carry
			     anything with them, so she is no caravan flier - the racing wings are
			     the mosquito's, not hers. -->
			<li>PMM_Gene_FlightWeak</li>
			<!-- The user's package, and its balance is the point: two evolutions
			     (serotonin, compound eyes) against two degrades (rapid life cycle,
			     microsized) - two and two, the balance VRE's own picker demands
			     (VRE_NeedEqualAmount). Microsized takes a flat 0.45 off her body
			     size, so she stands at 0.55 before anything else.
			     The trade to know about: serotonin keeps her blissful AND doubles her
			     chance of a social fight (`socialFightChanceFactor 2`, and its own
			     description promises the same). A hive full of happy, squabbling
			     farmers is the result, deliberately kept. -->
			<li>VRE_Serotonin</li>
			<li>VRE_CompoundEyes</li>
			<li>VRE_RapidLifeCycle</li>
			<li>VRE_Microsized</li>
			<!-- Her whole reason for existing: the hive's honey. The state and the
			     dials live on the gene (Defs/GeneDefs/Genes_Honey.xml), never on her
			     race, so another caste can be given honey later by one gene. -->
			<li>PMM_Gene_Honey</li>
			<!-- Vanilla genes in the user's words: "good plants" is
			     AptitudeStrong_Plants, "good animals" AptitudeStrong_Animals - both the
			     game's own TEMPLATE genes, one built per skill at load, so there is no
			     def to find in the files. "Poor intellect" is
			     AptitudePoor_Intellectual, "poor social" AptitudePoor_Social. -->
			<li>AptitudeStrong_Plants</li>
			<li>AptitudeStrong_Animals</li>
			<li>AptitudePoor_Intellectual</li>
			<li>AptitudePoor_Social</li>
			<!-- A worker bee does not breed (user's list): vanilla's `Sterile`, the same
			     barren lock the queen and four of her sisters carry, which works because
			     core's MomoFertilityPatch stands aside for a deliberate sterility. -->
			<li>Sterile</li>
		</genes>
		<modExtensions>
			<li Class="BigAndSmall.XenotypeExtension">
				<setRace>PMM_Race_HoneyBee</setRace>
				<forceRace>true</forceRace>
			</li>
			<li Class="PMM_Insects.InsectSkinColours">
				<colours>
					<li>PMM_Skin_BeeBright</li>
					<li>PMM_Skin_BeeVivid</li>
					<li>PMM_Skin_BeeGold</li>
				</colours>
			</li>
		</modExtensions>
	</XenotypeDef>

</Defs>
